# Jokers
A joker is a card, with what makes it a joker on top:  a subclass of `card`.
- It has no rank or suit, so it changes what those decided:  its value, its picture, its name and its short name.
- Everything else it gets from `card`:  it turns over, draws both its sides and drags as any card does.
- A deck holds its two only when it's made `with jokers`.  Solitaire's own game plays without them.

<spell-view "joker" template="card">
	<group "what's different" description="A joker comes red or black"/>
	<property "color" one-of="red or black"/>
	<alias "is the (color) joker"/>

	<group "what it changes" description="A card's own, written again for a joker"/>
	<property "value">
		53 if it is the red joker
		54 otherwise
	</property>
	<property "picture">
		return "🃟"
	</property>
	<property "name">its color + " joker"</>
	<property "state" description="Its short name:  *R↑ is the red joker, face up">
		letter is (the first letter of its color) as upper case
		arrow is "↑" if it is face up otherwise "↓"
		return "*" + letter + arrow
	</property>

	<test "jokers">
		get a new joker whose color is red and direction is up
		it is a card should be yes
		it is a joker should be yes
		its color should be red
		its name should be "red joker"
		its state should be "*R↑"
		its picture should be "🃟"
		it is the red joker should be yes
		it is the black joker should be no
		it is not the black joker should be yes

		// what it gets from card
		it is face up should be yes
		turn it over
		it is face down should be yes

		set black joker to a new joker whose color is black
		the picture of black joker should be "🃟"

		set the card to a new card whose rank is queen and suit is spades
		the card is a joker should be no
		the card is not a joker should be yes
		the card is the red joker should be no
	</test>
</spell-view>
